    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0042",
      "sequence": 54,
      "meaning": "The river of fame is lovely through all six seasons, beautiful in its time and deeply purifying. The marriage of Śiva with the Mountain’s daughter is its dewy winter; the Lord’s joyful birth is its pleasant cool season. The company at Rāma’s marriage, which I shall describe, is spring, king of seasons, filled with joy and auspiciousness. Rāma’s unbearable forest-going is summer, and the road’s events its scorching sun and wind. The terrible conflict with night-roamers is monsoon, bringing auspicious growth to the gods’ rice-crop. The joy, discipline and greatness of Rāma’s reign are its clear and pleasing autumn. The account of Sītā’s virtues, crown-jewel of faithful women, is its pure and incomparable water. Bharata’s nature is its coolness, always constant and beyond description. The mutual looks, words, meetings, affection and laughter and the fine brotherhood of the four brothers are the water’s sweetness and fragrance.",
